course: dictionary
lesson: 110
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Admiral can mean a very high-ranking officer who commands a navy's ships, or it can mean a butterfly. The context tells you which one. «Admiral Zheng He led seven great voyages with hundreds of ships.» Ships and voyages point to the navy meaning.
explain: Now look at this: «A red admiral landing on a rotting plum is tasting it as it lands.» A plum and a butterfly landing on it point to the insect. Always ask: which meaning fits the clues around the word? Then try that meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the words beside admiral too. Red admiral is a phrase, two words that go together to name one thing. Admiral alone usually means the officer, but red admiral names the butterfly.
fact: An admiral is a very high-ranking officer in a navy who commands many ships, called a fleet.
fact: A red admiral is a black butterfly with red bands and white spots on its wings.
fact: «Admiral Nelson» won the Battle of Trafalgar, and there is a column named after him in Trafalgar Square in London.
fact: Red admirals are common in gardens, often seen on buddleia and nettles.
fact: Red admiral caterpillars eat nettles, and the butterflies lay their eggs on nettles.
exercise: «Admiral Zheng He led seven great voyages with hundreds of ships.» In this sentence, what does admiral mean? | A ship's cook | A type of garden plant | *A high-ranking naval officer who commands ships | A black butterfly with red bands
exercise: «A red admiral landing on a rotting plum is tasting it as it lands.» What does admiral mean here? | *A butterfly with red bands and white spots | A kind of fruit | A large ship with many sailors | A navy officer in charge of a fleet
exercise: Which phrase names the butterfly, not the officer? | Vice admiral | Admiral Nelson | Rear admiral | *Red admiral
test: What do red admiral caterpillars eat? | Oak leaves | *Nettles | Buddleia | Roses
test: In «Admiral Nelson», which meaning of admiral is used? | A garden flower | *A high-ranking naval officer | A black butterfly | A kind of fruit
exam: When a word has more than one meaning, what is the best way to decide which one the writer means? | Guess the first meaning you learned | *Read the words around it and check which meaning fits the clues | Skip the word and never come back to it | Ignore the sentence and use only the title
